      "question": "Which clinical specialty should manage this patient?",
      "my_answer": "Ophthalmology (or primary care with ophthalmology backup).",
      "rationale": "Conjunctival disease is within ophthalmology scope; however, mild allergic conjunctivitis can be initially managed in primary care with referral if symptoms persist or worsen."
    },
    {
      "id": "Q4",
      "question": "What red‑flag findings would suggest a more serious ocular condition?",
      "my_answer": "Severe eye pain, photophobia, decreased visual acuity, purulent or mucopurulent discharge, corneal opacity/ulceration, elevated intra‑ocular pressure, unilateral severe redness, or pre‑auricular lymphadenopathy.",
      "rationale": "These features point toward keratitis, uveitis, acute angle‑closure glaucoma, or bacterial infection, which require urgent assessment."
    },
