      "my_answer": "Viral conjunctivitis, bacterial conjunctivitis, irritant (chemical) conjunctivitis, atopic keratoconjunctivitis, and early uveitis.",
      "rationale": "All can cause red, watery eyes, but differ in discharge type, pain, laterality, and associated symptoms; the absence of pain, purulent discharge, and unilateral findings favors allergic etiology."
    },
    {
